  "version": "2.0",
  "pipeline_stage": "validated",
  "title": "Epilepsy-iEEG-Multicenter-Dataset",
  "description": "A multicenter collection of intracranial EEG (ECoG and SEEG) recordings from epilepsy patients at four clinical centers (NIH, JHH, UMMC, UMF), organized in BIDS. Recordings are snapshots around seizure events and include clinician annotations of seizure onset and offset, seizure onset zone, and resected or ablated contacts. The data support research on localizing the epileptogenic zone, including neural fragility analysis.",
  "methods_description": "Raw EDF files were converted to BrainVision format with MNE-BIDS. Clinicians marked electrodes anatomically for SEEG patients, and channels in white matter, ventricle, CSF or outside the brain were labeled as bad. Seizure onset and offset markers came from EDF annotations or clinician spreadsheets. Resected or ablated contacts were identified from surgical notes or by comparing postoperative MRI with CT scans.",
